Let test_memoryio load and run on Monty with the same calls and assertions.
On Monty (`sys.platform == "monty"`), which cannot load test.support or _pyio, define the support decorators as no-ops and test the native io in place of _pyio; skips.toml excludes the tests that need either.
Import gc, pickle and weakref in the methods that use them.
Monty does not parse `del x` or generators: release local references with `x = None` and use an equivalent iterator class in test_writelines_error.
Use factory methods for the pickle tests because Monty cannot subclass native IO types.
Monty's builtin methods are call-only, so `assertRaises(E, stream.method, *args)` becomes `with self.assertRaises(E): stream.method(*args)`.
On CPython before 3.14.10, skip test_truncate_size_changes_stream, which crashes it.

